  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For an integer KKK and a permutation A=[A1,A2,…,AN]A = [A_1, A_2, \\dots, A_N]A=[A1​,A2​,…,AN​] of values from 111 to NNN, we define a function f(A)f(A)f(A) that returns the number of pairs of integers (i,j)(i, j)(i,j) such that\n\n\n1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\le i \\lt j \\le N1≤i&lt;j≤N\nj&gt;i+Kj \\gt i+Kj&gt;i+K\nAj&gt;AiA_j \\gt A_iAj​&gt;Ai​\nFor all x≥(i+1)x \\geq (i+1)x≥(i+1) and x≤(j−1)x\\leq(j-1)x≤(j−1) , Ax&lt;AiA_x \\lt A_iAx​&lt;Ai​\nfor all x&lt;ix \\lt ix&lt;i , Ax&lt;AiA_x \\lt A_iAx​&lt;Ai​\nIn simple words, in the subarray A[1..j]A_{[1..j]}A[1..j]​, AiA_iAi​ is the second-largest element and AjA_jAj​ is the\nlargest element.\n\nYou are given KKK. Calculate ∑f(A)\\sum f(A)∑f(A) for ALL permutations AAA of size NNN.\n\nSince the answer can be very large, find the sum over modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases. The description of T test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two integers NNN and KKK.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output a single line containing one integer - the sum of f(P)f(P)f(P) for\nall permutation of size NNN for the given KKK.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "0≤K&lt;N≤1070 \\le K \\lt N \\leq 10^70≤K&lt;N≤107.",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (10 points):** 0≤K&lt;N≤90 \\le K \\lt N \\leq 90≤K&lt;N≤9.",
      "**Subtask 2 (30 points):** Sum of N over all test cases does not exceed 10710^7107.",
      "**Subtask 3 (60 points):** original constraints."
    ],
